# Build output
bin/
obj/

# Visual Studio
.vs/
*.user
*.suo
*.userosscache
*.sln.docstates

# Test results
TestResults/
*.trx
*.coverage
*.coveragexml

# The build-and-test workflow's Test step tees the run's output here, at the
# checkout root, so it can grep it for a passing count. Harmless on a runner,
# an untracked file for anyone reproducing the steps locally.
test-output.txt

# The survivors exhibit writes its SVG to stdout and every documented
# invocation redirects it - `survivors > survivors.svg` in README.md and in
# Program.cs's own usage - so running the exhibit as instructed, from the
# checkout root, dirties the tree. That is a defect of the instructions rather
# than of anyone's conduct, and this is the fix.
#
# Anchored and prefixed on purpose, not a blanket *.svg: an exhibit SVG
# committed deliberately - under docs/, or at any other path - stays tracked,
# and only the output the documented redirect produces at the root is ignored.
# Use `git add -f` if one of these ever is meant to be kept.
/survivors*.svg

# The same, for the `deep` subcommand: README.md and Program.cs's own usage
# redirect it as `deep 3 4 13 > deep3.svg`, which the line above does not match
# - it is anchored AND prefixed, and that prefix is `survivors`. Named here on
# the same terms rather than by widening the line above to `*.svg`, for the
# reason that line already gives: a blanket pattern would swallow an exhibit
# somebody meant to commit.
/deep*.svg

# NuGet packages
*.nupkg
*.snupkg

# OS files
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store

# Local agent-harness settings. Per-machine and per-operator, not this repo's
# to carry.
.claude/
